  "slug": "automated-enables-08a1",
  "summary": "New preprints pair automated acquisition with multimodal registration, from reusable Patch-seq pipettes to whole-bulb glomerular maps and MALDI-fluorescence fusion.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is scaling quantitative cell characterization through automation and multimodal registration. In Patch-seq, detergent-cleaned reusable pipettes, robotic nucleus extraction and sonication preserve electrophysiology and transcriptomic yield, a stated foundation for automated profiling. Probabilistic C. elegans head-neuron atlases built from near-wild-type strains reach 86.3% top-1 variability-aware identification. Whole-bulb light-sheet expansion microscopy with automated segmentation maps thousands of glomeruli in intact mouse olfactory bulbs. SCOUBI infers axon-dendrite interfaces from extrasomatic transcripts in mouse brain spatial transcriptomics. A second strand fuses imaging modalities: MeXalign coregisters LA-ICP-TOFMS and immunofluorescence via segmentation masks, and FluoMALDI links fluorescence-defined genes, proteins and organelles to spatial lipid composition. Disease- and glia-focused tools add 3D readouts: PASTA resolves amyloid-beta lesion heterogeneity, growth lineages and microglial contacts, and PolyMorph3D quantifies microglia morphology with colocalization of up to four markers. Two methodologically related works fall outside neural tissue: MiSA detects spatial dysbiosis in oral biofilms, and stitched montage cryo-ET maps connected Arp2/3 actin networks in lamellipodia.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
